From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0170-native-storage-buffer-pointer-tracking.patch

Source: 0170-native-storage-buffer-pointer-tracking.patch
Moved by hand: the compute binding's native flag is upstream's IsDlssDispatch() now (our 0322 is in v1.219.020)

Port of Orchid 812a4e1eb by MythosOfs, from zortos293/Eglantine: Duck912 and
zortos293 (9e56ed7b2, 560b4c0bd, f6a8f5132, 8644f32fb, 448fdaed9, 546cb6782),
Jonas (d854ff0de), Duck912 (f9acc60a5). Adds paired, atomic and loaded pointer
tracking and pointer table bindings (indirect_offset) for native programs.
NVN programs keep the old search.

Differences from the source: this core already had the first candidate
tracking, the environment's pointer map and its serialization, so only the rest
is added. Orchid's pruned search is left out; the plain search stays. A table
binding uses the native size rule (no NVN size word), capped at 8 MiB here; 0104
raises that. GLSL and GLASM do not read indirect pointers, as in the source.

Pipeline cache versions Vulkan 23, OpenGL 20: an old list lacks the new
classifications and FileEnvironment would throw.

Two things are ours, not the source's. EDEN_NX2_NATIVE_TABLES=0 turns off every
pointer read through memory (indirect_offset): table entries and single ones,
compute and graphics. Default on, as in the source. The rest of the tracking has
no switch. And a program can no longer pass the 32 storage buffer bindings: the
pass stops there and leaves the rest global, table entries leave room for the
NVN slots the program reads, and AddNVNStorageBuffers stops when full. Each case
logs a warning.
